course: dictionary
lesson: 9364
title: Spongy and the clues around it
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: You do not need to know every word to understand a text. Read the words around an unknown word, because they leave clues. «Baobabs store thousands of litres of water in their huge spongy trunks.» A trunk that stores lots of water must have room inside it, so spongy must mean soft and full of tiny holes.
explain: Check your meaning by putting it into the sentence. A trunk that is soft and full of tiny holes can hold water, so the meaning makes sense. Spongy also describes ground that is soft and wet, the way a marsh feels under your feet.
explain: A word can also describe how something feels when you press it. A spongy thing is squashy and springs back when pressed. If brakes feel spongy, they have too much give, so they may not stop you well.
fact: Spongy means soft, squashy and full of tiny holes, like a sponge.
fact: A spongy thing springs back when you press it.
fact: Spongy can describe ground that is soft and wet.
fact: Spongy can also describe brakes that have too much give.
fact: «Felt-tip pens have a spongy core soaked in ink that feeds the tip.»
exercise: «Baobabs store thousands of litres of water in their huge spongy trunks.» What does spongy mean here? | *Soft and full of tiny holes | Very cold | Bright and shiny | Hard as stone
exercise: Lena presses a sponge and it springs back. What does spongy mean? | *Soft, squashy and springs back when pressed | Wet with sea water only | Very tall | Hard and rigid like a brick
exercise: Mum says the brakes on the bike feel spongy. What does that suggest? | They are painted red | *They have too much give and may not stop well | They make a loud noise | They stop very quickly and firmly
test: «Rice can grow in flooded fields because air passes down spongy tubes in its stems to the roots.» What does spongy most likely mean here? | Painted green | *Soft and full of tiny holes that let air pass through | Solid and heavy like metal | Frozen solid
test: Which description fits spongy ground? | Ground that is hard, dry and cracked | Ground made of ice | *Ground that is soft and wet, so your feet sink in a little | Ground covered in bricks
exam: Tom says a spongy cake is heavy and hard as a rock. Which answer is best? | Tom is right: spongy means hard and heavy | Tom is right: spongy means wet and cold | *Tom is wrong: spongy means soft and light | Tom is wrong: spongy means sharp and pointed
